// Package store tests — T-20 characterization (Phase 2).
//
// THE LAW (roadmap Phase 2 + task list standing orders): the Python
// characterization tests are ported FIRST, then the code; the goldens were
// GENERATED by running the unmodified Python reference app
// (assadigit/GitCurator @ 98f4fc7) via testdiff/goldens/dump_store.py —
// never hand-typed. Regenerate with:
//
//	python3 testdiff/goldens/dump_store.py
//
// Ported/landed suites:
//   - The timestamp grammar corpus (generated; pins datetime.isoformat()
//     shapes — the ADR-0003 decision-4 naive/UTC string laws).
//   - THE T-20 ACCEPTANCE: opening a real Python-created cache.db fixture
//     passes read/write probes; WAL mode asserted (task list T-20 row).
//   - The sqlite-level shadow-cache assertions DEFERRED from T-12
//     (SESSION-004): Python test_phase0.py
//     test_shadow_cache_reads_real_state_writes_are_discarded — "the
//     shadow sees the real rows / writes land in the shadow only" — now
//     provable with a real SQLite handle through modernc.
//   - THE SQLITE LAW concurrency port (tests/test_syncreview.py
//     TestLedgerConcurrency.test_two_threads_mark_the_same_db shape):
//     several handles on one file get a clean wait (busy_timeout + WAL),
//     never an error. Its test_locking_law_in_source twin is realized as
//     the DSN/pragma assertions below (Go source obviously differs from
//     Python source text).
//   - test_close_is_idempotent (same file's TestDeferredLog).
//
// The fixture (testdata/cache_python_created.db) and its content golden
// are an ATOMIC PAIR: regeneration rewrites both together (the reference's
// own now() timestamps necessarily change per run); fixture_sha256 in the
// golden ties the pair, and this suite verifies the tie.
